  {
   "block": "explain",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "figures": {},
     "literals": [
      "1",
      "2016",
      "FY2017"
     ],
     "text": "A season runs from 1 January to 1 November. What a senior earns comes off the third-quarter tax bill of the next fiscal year, so the 2016 season is charged to FY2017."
    },
    {
     "figures": {},
     "literals": [
      "2014"
     ],
     "text": "Since 2014 a senior in the program is paid as a town employee, and federal tax, Medicare and retirement are withheld. It is the **net** pay that is credited, so the cap is the most a senior can earn, not the reduction on the bill."
    },
    {
     "figures": {},
     "literals": [],
     "text": "Every figure here is a total for all participants. No participant is named and no one’s amount is shown."
    }
   ],
   "place": "lead",
   "title": "How a season is counted",
   "tone": "define"
  },
